WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.600
Speaker 1: Hey, David, we see more and more
sexual assault allegations and sexual harassment

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.029
allegations against candidates, and it seems
to matter less than ever.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:12.730
Do voters even care about sexual harassment
anymore?

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:17.960
I think that this is an interesting question
for a couple of different reasons.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:25.169
It does seem as though lately candidates and
other prominent people get hit with allegations

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:27.960
of sexual harassment or sexual assault.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.070
They don't drop out or resign or go into therapy
or whatever.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.700
You know, there's different ways that it's
sometimes handled and they still sort of do

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.700
OK.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.700
I mean, Donald Trump is example.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:43.660
No one accused by, you know, 16 to 48 different
women at different points in time and didn't

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.220
drop out and was elected president, period.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.430
There was that special election in Alabama
where Republican Roy Moore, who was accused

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.910
of harassing underage women, lost by only
a point and a half in twenty seventeen.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:01.370
Now a Republican losing by one point five
and in Alabama is a big deal because it's

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.400
such a red state.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.730
But it didn't completely knock him out of
the running.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.150
If a couple of things went a little differently,
he still would have won.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:15.520
Andrew Cuomo, he has been accused of all sorts
of improper touching and a verbal comments

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.010
by multiple women.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.720
He has said, at least for now, he's not going
to resign, even if he's not cleared by the

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.460
attorney general report.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:28.590
He's made public appearances with other legislative
leaders, some of whom called for him to resign.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.070
But about half of New Yorkers don't think
he should resign.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.820
That includes 61 percent of Democrats.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.000
It's still currently under the investigation
phase.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.090
But we've seen people resign during investigations
before and it's not clear it's having a major

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.090
impact.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:46.220
Some of the covid mishandling is with the
nursing home scandal we talked about previously.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:48.880
But he's just still kicking around Matt Gates.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.770
Now, Matt Gates allegedly paid for sex from
underage women for whom he paid to go from

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:58.670
one state to another, which legally counts
as sex trafficking.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:02.020
Not facing too many calls to resign.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:06.220
The Republican caucus is basically behind
him.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.280
It's not clear whether it's going to affect
him unless he's actually charged.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.190
And even then, we're going to wait and see.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:16.900
During the Brett Kavanaugh confirmation hearings
to the Supreme Court, he maintained very high

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.170
Republican support.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:27.900
After Christine Blazey Blazey, Ford testified
Brett Kavanaugh's approval from Republicans

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.180
went up, even if I recall correctly.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:33.260
So there's a couple of different things going
on here.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:38.480
We sort of knew a lot of people didn't really
care.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:44.400
But increasingly, it seems as though it's
not playing a role in politics where there

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.370
are more people taking the approach of it.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:52.880
Depends who you talk to, but a lot of Democrats
taking the approach of if Republicans aren't

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.180
going to hold them accountable, why are we
going to go crazy?

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.820
The Al Franken situation comes to mind where
compared to the things Republicans have been

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.760
accused of and just stuck it out.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.670
Al Franken resignation is now seen as premature
by many, given what he was accused of.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.730
An untasteful joke for for tasteless joke.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.190
No, no doubt about it.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:16.040
But comparatively, you've seen a lot of Democrats
say, hey, let's not go crazy because they're

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.129
not doing anything about these allegations
on their side.

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:20.709
I think Republican voters genuinely don't
care.

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:26.450
They have taken a sort of greater good mentality
of, yeah, even if we're evangelical Christians,

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.709
we'll still elect the guy with the multiple
wives and the cheating and the divorce and

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:34.050
the mistresses and whatever, because Democrats
are just worse in general and they support

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.819
abortion and whatever.

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:37.310
So they justify it that way.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:43.599
So I think that while individuals in their
lives care about sexual harassment and sexual

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:50.900
assault, I think politically it is less of
a successful or effective hatchet to end someone's

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.900
career.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:57.510
And that's a result both of some aspects from
the right and some aspects from the left,

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:02.800
although the left has been far more consistent
when it came to Al Franken, Anthony Weiner

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:08.599
in just abandoning the accused people, I think
some sort of realpolitik type, pragmatic perspective

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:14.599
lately is making even some on the left reconsider
whether we should just leave the sexual harassment

00:04:14.599 --> 00:04:20.239
to that's the personal life of the individual
and at least claim that it has nothing to

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:23.470
do with their actions as an elected official

